{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-8","id":"msg_016VNCu73BK3rcCoQ6oxm6EE","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"**Anchor** is a single-folder, local-first personal productivity system for J.C. Liechty, built almost entirely on Python stdlib. Grounded claims about what it is and ships:\n\n- **A markdown-backed task/project manager.** The source of truth is plain markdown files (`DASHBOARD.md`, `PROJECTS.md`, `INBOX.md`, `domains/*.md`, plus `CANCELLED.md`/`SAVED_FOR_LATER.md` archives). Tasks move through a lifecycle â€” active â†’ done â†’ cancelled â†’ saved â†’ restored â€” with priority, energy, domain, due-date, and notes fields.\n\n- **It ships two interfaces over the same logic.** `anchor_gui.py` is the primary app: a self-contained stdlib HTTP server that renders the full dashboard HTML and writes markdown directly via a REST-style API. `anchor.py` is a CLI mirror (same parsing/format) that also regenerates the static `dashboard.html`.\n\n- **It runs as a persistent local service.** The server is owned by the NSSM Windows service `anchor` (auto-start), binds `http://localhost:8777` with an exclusive-bind single-instance guard, and is restarted via `nssm restart anchor` â€” not launched by hand.\n\n- **It self-tests daily.** `anchor_healthcheck.py` runs at 5:00 AM via Task Scheduler: it parses every markdown file, boots a throwaway server, exercises every endpoint and task state, walks the v2/v3/v4 R&D surfaces fully stubbed (never live `claude`, never port 8777), and writes a dated report to `health_reports/`.\n\n- **Its largest subsystem is an \"R&D Control Surface\" for trio-driven development.** Each project gets a window that manages work across lanes (Research Â· Planning Â· Build Â· Deliverables Â· Grass Catchers), built in four iterative versions:\n  - **v2** â€” session model, cached/validated AI summaries, grass-catcher ideas, deliverable pinning, an interactive terminal substrate.\n  - **v3 \"Mission Control\"** â€” real ConPTY terminals (the one declared native exception, `pywinpty`), per-session git-worktree isolation, a stacking window manager, stage handoffs, runnable deliverable previews, and Ghost World Labs branding.\n  - **v4 \"Project Cockpit\"** (built + merged to master 2026-06-13) â€” a single seeded ConPTY terminal substrate (skill auto-loads/greets once, killing the repeating-prompt bug), a Claudeâ†”Gemini engine toggle, Paradigm-2 inline expanding lane tiles with status lights, per-lane doc roles, project cost/tokens/time rollups, grass-to-lane promotion, and type-aware deliverable launch.\n\n- **It orchestrates a planning/build \"trio.\"** The R&D surface launches the trio skills â€” researchPrime (research) â†’ Crucible (planning) â†’ Foreman (build) â€” as durable, isolated server-side terminal sessions, with a North Star of making each project window a calm, single-screen cockpit where opening a session \"feels exactly like a normal Claude Code / Gemini session.\"\n\n- **Hard constraint: stdlib-only, no binaries, fully file-accessible.** One declared exception (`pywinpty`, lazy, terminal-only, optional `pip install .[terminal]`); `distro.py` enforces this by refusing any other native/third-party import. Everything stays plain text so it remains usable from Claude Code, the CLI, or any tool."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":4253,"cache_creation_input_tokens":24733,"cache_read_input_tokens":20597,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":24733},"output_tokens":2,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"c4fa01c3-7509-4ee8-8c6d-2d3f37179222","uuid":"a61ad17a-304a-44d9-b32e-2ca237b58985","request_id":"req_011Cc1nT3DNfGTvijBz73ZYV"}
